Changes made to PCB design: 

Updated capacitor location and created fills to match datasheet recommendations for buck converter

Changed 5V line to 6V line. Motor, servo, and solenoids all run at 6V, and buck converter can take 6V as input. No changes to layout. 

Added touchscreen and SD card connections, removed two buttons and one led from previous user IO

Notes: 
We are using GPIO45 for the touch interrupt input. GPIO45 is a strapping input, and should be left floating on startup. However, 
It should be able to be configured to digital input after startup. I have left the GPIO pin disconnected but it can be shorted to 
the touch interrupt input IRQ_TOUCH through the headers. 
